'''NOPW Wednesday Episode 13''' was the thirteenth weekly [[Wednesday Night Wrestling|Wednesday night]] professional wrestling event produced by [[New Okaiken Pro-Wrestling|NOPW]], held on November 4, 2026 at the Tosa Prefectural Arena in [[Tosa]] — the second repeat market of the series' second season. The show was the Power Struggle build's escalation night, headlined by G1 winner [[Marcus Vance]] defeating [[Kengo Vaiahi|Kengo]] in the main event — and by what happened after the bell, when the champion himself came down to protect the road to [[Wrestling Summit 2027|Wrestling Summit]].

== Background ==

One week into the Power Struggle build, the November card was taking shape and the Wednesday product was settling into its second season. The storylines entering Episode 13:

* '''The truth against the artist.''' Jusuf's welcome for Nakamura Shinsuke — ''"Art is a lie with good lighting. In November, I turn off the lights."'' — awaited an answer.
* '''The tag war.''' Kuroshio and the champions had brawled backstage at Episode 12; the title match was official. The six-man tag on this show would be the last word before Power Struggle.
* '''Kengo's descent.''' The chair attack on Taumafa at Episode 12 demanded a response — and a sanction.
* '''The young lions' November.''' Iwata and Yamamoto, robbed of the junior tag titles by tights and ropes, needed momentum for the rematch.

