== Match details ==

* '''Match 1:''' Face against face — the young lions against the mutineers, two teams the Cannon Club used to own. Clean, fast, competitive; the springboard DDT on Riku at 12:33. Handshakes after — the Usos raised the young lions' hands themselves. '''Crowd:''' dueling POP. '''USO''' and '''SEIGIGUN''' chants. The rematch momentum belongs to Iwata and Yamamoto.
* '''Match 2:''' The artist's tune-up. Nakamura played with Morita for nine minutes — the knee tremors, the taunts, the Boma Ye at 9:58. Jusuf watched from the top of the ramp the entire match, motionless, the Intercontinental Championship on his shoulder. '''Crowd:''' '''NAKAMURA''' chants. The quiet under the fun — the truth-teller does not laugh.
* '''Match 3:''' The television title — the junior tag champion moving up for a shot, and finding the Ishida Lock waiting. The '''ninth''' submission of the reign, at 11:26. '''Crowd:''' '''ISHIDA''' chants. HEAT for the champions' corner work. The open challenge stands: nine have come, nine have tapped.
* '''Match 4:''' The last word before Power Struggle — three-quarters of Kuroshio (the three who are not the champion) against the tag champions and Fujinami. The champions' frustration went from ambush to collapse: Kuroki's Black Iron clothesline flattened Reyes at 17:41. The arms-crossed pose, three abreast. '''Crowd:''' '''KUROSHIO''' chants. STANDING OVATION. The champions left arguing.
* '''Match 5:''' The family's answer. One week after the chair, Taumafa defended the Strong Openweight title like nothing happened — the hip attack, the corner splash, the Samoan driver at 8:05. And then Kengo appeared on the screen: unhinged, alone, laughing. ''"You carry the family's belt. I AM the family. At Power Struggle — no disqualification. Come and carry it from me."'' Taumafa took the mic: ''"Come and try."'' '''Crowd:''' '''TAUMAFA''' chants. HEAT for the screen. The no-disqualification match is on.
* '''Match 6:''' The main event — the abandonment comes home. The man Kengo left against the leader who left everyone. Kengo's chaos and shortcuts against the work: the slide-off, the 44 Calibre, the Drill Driver at 15:52. And then Kengo took the chair anyway. One shot across Vance's back before the officials moved — and Leoni Masua's music hit. Kengo fled through the crowd. The champion walked to the ring, took the chair, folded it, and set it down beside the G1 winner. He looked at Vance on one knee — and said one line: ''"Not before Toyozawa."'' Then he left. Vance got up alone. '''Crowd:''' the loudest moment of the night — ERUPTION for the music, SILENCE for the line, then '''LEONI''' chants as he walked out. Vance's stare followed him up the ramp.

== The confrontation (after Match 2) ==

With Jusuf still on the ramp, Nakamura Shinsuke took the microphone and answered the welcome:

''"He says art is a lie with good lighting. He says he will turn off the lights."'' A pause. The grin. ''"Then I will paint in the dark. COME ON."''

Jusuf said nothing. He raised the Intercontinental Championship once, set it on his shoulder, and left. The first face-to-face of the truth against the artist — no contact, all signal.

'''Crowd:''' '''NAKAMURA''' chants. HEAT following Jusuf up the ramp.

== Storyline notes ==

* '''The Power Struggle card is nearly complete:''' Jusuf (c) vs. Nakamura Shinsuke (Intercontinental); Kuroshio vs. Reyes & Kimura (c) (tag); Taumafa (c) vs. Kengo, '''no disqualification''' (Strong Openweight); Ishida's open challenge (television); and the junior tag rematch owed to Iwata & Yamamoto.
* '''The champion protects the match, not the man.''' Leoni's first appearance since Episode 12 was one line and one folded chair. The road to Toyozawa is his to guard — even from Kengo.
* '''The artist answers.''' Nakamura will paint in the dark. Jusuf said nothing at all — which, from Jusuf, is the loudest thing.
* '''Nine have come, nine have tapped.''' Ishida's television reign is becoming a ledger.
* '''Kuroshio's November.''' The six-man statement — with Maeda beside them — makes the brothers the story of the tag division, and the champions' collapse the undercard tragedy.

